SM-T715 tablet: no phone leftovers in the user's setup or the shell log.

The owner's Lenovomarchy port's 0004-tablet-phone-leftovers, reworded, with
two changes for this tablet:
- omamobile-setup-user's steps never add the plugins this build does not
  ship (fingerprint, update, access, mobilenetwork), remove them and
  their links and menu rows from a user an earlier build set up; quick
  settings never probe the hardware of a tile the catalogue dropped
  (omamobile-gnss, omamobile-fp-enroll, rfkill's nfc line, brightnessctl's
  torch). omamobile.call is shipped again (the arm64 image has the modem
  stack now; its UI patches are 0010-0013 and the call card's Speaker
  toggle is hidden in 0013), and so is omamobile.voice (the voice bar;
  0014 makes it hear other languages than English): their steps below add
  them, Setup > Voice and the Voxtype setup as upstream's do, and the
  cleanup pass leaves them, their links and Setup > Voice alone. The
  launcher loads the voice link as upstream's does (Lenovomarchy's guard
  for a missing voice plugin is not carried: the plugin ships).
- SM-T715: the suspend-off step stays upstream's (the arm64 image masks the
  sleep targets, and sets the toggle at build time); Lenovomarchy's removes
  the toggle, for its tablet's verified s2idle.
- SM-T715: the guard on a dropped tile's refresh takes the catalogue id
  (tileRefresh(tile, "rotation-lock")): Lenovomarchy's read tile.id, which a
  QML object's id is not, and its rotation guard asked for "rotationLock";
  harmless there (both tiles dropped), it would stop the Rotation tile that
  this build keeps from ever reading its state.
Against omarchy-mobile 8991845 (omamobile-shell 0.2.147), after 0001-0003.

